---
import '../posters.css';
import AdFooter from '../AdFooter.astro';

export const ad = {
  slug: "square-glasses",
  title: "The Noun in the square glasses.",
  description: "He has not taken them off since the day he arrived.",
  art: "/ad-department/art/car.svg",
};
---

<article class="campaign-ad" aria-labelledby="ad-glasses">
  <div class="ad-folio">Advertisement</div>
  <div class="ad-inner">
    <div class="ad-visual" style="background: #d5d7e1">
      <img
        src="/ad-department/art/car.svg"
        alt="A Noun with a red car for a head, wearing square black glasses"
        class="noun"
        style="position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 50%; height: 88%; transform: translateX(-50%)"
      />
    </div>
    <p class="ad-caption">He has not taken them off since the day he arrived.</p>
    <h2 id="ad-glasses" class="ad-headline">
      The Noun in the square glasses.
    </h2>
    <div class="ad-copy cols-3">
      <p>
        He turned up at the garage on a Tuesday, thirty-two pixels tall, with a car where his head
        should be. Nobody asked. In El Segundo it is considered rude to.
      </p>
      <p>
        The glasses are square because the buildings are square. He will tell you a curve is only
        a straight line that lost its nerve.
      </p>
      <p>
        He belongs to nobody. The lawyers call it CC0, which means he is yours, and ours, and the
        mechanic&rsquo;s, in the way that weather is.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most afternoons you will find him out front beside the gold Ferrari, looking at the wall
        behind it. He says the wall is the better picture. He may be right.
      </p>
    </div>
    <AdFooter>Brutalist motor art.<br />Looked at properly.</AdFooter>
  </div>
</article>
